  "goodToKnow": "Die Kleinstadt is a small town; officially, one with 5,000 to 20,000 inhabitants. Larger ones are a Mittelstadt (20,000–100,000) and a Großstadt (over 100,000). Germany is a country of Kleinstädte, many with a medieval centre, a Marktplatz and a church. Kleinstädtisch can mean provincial or narrow-minded. Das Kleinstadtleben is small-town life. Plural: die Kleinstädte."
